  "evidenceClassification": "Executed service/storage/runtime/telemetry tests using synthetic non-media source metadata, non-executable test tool files and injected EventEmitter children. Not actual FFmpeg execution or retained media qualification.",
  "cleanup": {
    "registration": "Immediately after creating the owned temporary directory, before fixture setup",
    "verification": "Close initialized service/storage/runtime resources, verify exact owned directory and parent, then remove only that directory",
    "historicalSetupLeak": "Five initial failed-setup directories were individually verified by exact inventory, fixture bytes, no symlinks and timestamps, then removed. Prior failed receipts retained."
  },
  "testCoverage": [
    "Real service selection to exact derived storage forecast and persisted reservation",
    "Actual runner timeout greater than legacy input and bounded by derived operation deadline",
    "Video telemetry record ceilings of 1280 and 20224 accepted, each first excess row rejected",
    "Sparse telemetry logical file size above derived ceiling rejected before parsing",
    "Storage pressure that permits legacy 32 MiB but exceeds derived reservation refused before encode",
    "Aggregate stdout/stderr callback at exact derived pipe allowance then one extra byte refused",
    "Real selector invalidation refused before reservation or encode",
    "Successful telemetry cases reach the unchanged collector refusal, with drained fake children, unchanged source and no published MKV"
  ],
  "qualificationLimits": [
    "Only video-stream record ceilings are stressed; audio contributes one valid row. Limits are per stream, not aggregate.",
    "Sparse-byte test proves logical file-size admission refusal, not streaming byte-counter enforcement.",
    "Fake runner callbacks exercise service aggregate pipe accounting without allocating or transferring that volume.",
    "Deadline routing is checked, not elapsed timer expiry. Live storage monitor and cancellation drainage are not exercised here.",
    "Closed collector prevents downstream decoded-evidence and child-count exhaustion coverage for this family.",
    "Synthetic successful telemetry ends with expected collector refusal, not media validation or output publication.",
    "No production source, factory gate, pin, retained qualification, runtime installation, default, UI or release change.",
    "Broad Linux result remains the previous failed 150/177 run, not rerun for this test-only delta. No native Windows, GPU or actual-media qualification."
  ],
  "receiptInterpretation": "dirtyPaths counts include pre-existing untracked excluded historical material. Exact production hashes and tracked diff establish no production change; test counts are separate suites and not additive.",
